 ### Encode thread
 
-The app turns the game's graphics commands into Metal commands on a thread of its own instead of the game's submitting thread, so the game's thread can go on sooner (in Breath of the Wild about 4 ms per frame instead of 8). Frame buffering needs it for games that present their frames from another thread than the one that draws them. It is on by default on the iPhone; on the Mac it is off, where it lowered the typical frame time but made the slowest frames slower.
+The app turns the game's graphics commands into Metal commands on a thread of its own instead of the game's submitting thread, so the game's thread can go on sooner (in Breath of the Wild about 4 ms per frame instead of 8). Frame buffering needs it for games that present their frames from another thread than the one that draws them. It is off by default (nxkit: games ran worse with it on the iPhone; it is no longer in the launcher, `DM_NVN_ENC_THREAD=1` in env.txt turns it on); on the Mac it lowered the typical frame time but made the slowest frames slower.
 
 - **When to change it:** leave it on unless a game misbehaves with it; turning it off is a diagnostic step.
 
